  "verbalization": "Montelukast, a leukotriene receptor antagonist, is implicated in the pathogenesis of allergic asthma through its effects on inflammatory mediators. The visible evidence suggests that Montelukast may be repurposed for the treatment of allergic asthma, as it is linked to indications for Vasomotor Rhinitis and Allergic Asthma through a chain of medications such as Flunisolide and Fluticasone Furoate. These corticosteroids are known to reduce inflammation in allergic conditions, and their association with allergic asthma implies a potential anti-inflammatory mechanism. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, highlighting a possible role of Montelukast in modulating inflammatory pathways that contribute to allergic asthma. The integration of these pathways suggests that Montelukast may exert a therapeutic effect by targeting inflammatory mediators, potentially offering a novel or expanded use in the management of allergic asthma.",
